{
  "_comment": "Multi-turn intake cases. The harness plays the student with FIXED scripted replies (never a model): turn 1 sends `opening`; each time the coach asks, the next entry of `replies` is sent (then `fallback_reply` once they run out). Like the app, durable notes the engine emits on a turn are appended to the ledger/profile sent on the next turn. questions = [min, max] clarifying questions a good coach asks before building the plan (the engine forces a plan at 5 user turns). answered = facts the student has given: `turn` is the user message index that supplied it (0 = opening, -1 = ledger/profile) and `ask` is a regex matching a coach question that asks for it again (checked case-insensitively on questions asked after that turn). expected_notes = facts (only scored when the user message `from_turn` that states them was actually sent) the extractor should record across the conversation: field notes|userNotes|any, optional sections, and keyword groups (all groups must match one note; any word within a group). forbidden_user_notes = task-specific words that must NOT land in the global user profile. forbidden_notes = facts already in the ledger that must not be re-recorded. plan_mentions = keyword groups (each {groups, from_turn}) that should each appear in some plan step title (deterministic proxy for 'plan uses the answers'); plan_forbidden = regexes no step title may match (e.g. redoing finished work); plan_max_minutes = a stated per-step limit. plan_forbidden entries are a regex or {regex, from_turn}; plan_max_minutes is {max, from_turn}.",
  "cases": [
